          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: હવામાન",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હવામાન — havāmān — \"weather, climate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "કાલે હવામાન સારું હશે. — kāle havāmān sārũ haśe — \"The weather will be good tomorrow.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હવામાન (havāmān) is built from two older words: havā, \"air\", a loan from Arabic hawā', which reached Gujarati through Persian (Lane, under the root h-w-y), and mān, \"measure\", from Sanskrit māna. CDIAL has no entry for the compound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
