          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઠંડું (ṭhanḍũ) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. CDIAL lists it, glossed \"cold\", under stabdha, \"firmly fixed; stiff; solidified (as water)\", by way of a reshaped ṭhaṇḍha-, so cold is what has set hard (CDIAL 13676)."
            }
